From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] core and server: the disk grid on the I/O worker, and a quiesce drain test

Two host gates the port shipped without, both from our fork `ai-engine` at
fork-ssh/ovn-up.

zig/src/core/rows_test.zig, the fork's hunks unchanged. Every case in the file sets
`sync_writes = true` (its `options` helper, line 18), so the grid round trip only ever
covered the writer that runs on the caller's thread. GLM's store uses the other one:
lane_host_rows.zig steps the I/O worker when `!r.sync_writes`. The fork turns the test
body into `gridRoundTrip(sync, tag)`, drains with
`rows.write.drain(r, rows.write.nowNs() + 3 s)` instead of the file's
`while (rows.write.step(r)) {}` helper, and adds a second case with the worker. The
original test keeps its name and calls the helper with true.

zig/src/server/health_test.zig and a new zig/src/server/health_quiesce_test.zig. `quiesce`
spun with a 5 second panic and no test ever made a connection outlive the accept loop, so
nothing proved that quiesce waits before the server is freed. This takes the fork's change
to quiesce (the wall-clock panic goes: a loaded host makes the wait slower, never wrong),
its `dial` and `closeAfter` helpers and its test, which opens a bare socket, waits for
`open_connections` to rise, closes it from another thread after 200 ms, and asserts
`open_connections` is zero the moment quiesce returns.

The fork puts that test in health_test.zig. Ours is 558 lines and tools/zig/lean_check.py
fails any file in zig/ over 600, so the fork's shape would make 611 and cost the lean gate
a new problem. The test and its two helpers go in health_quiesce_test.zig instead,
registered beside health_test.zig in zig/src/server/root.zig's test block, and
health_test.zig ends at 556: the only changes left in it are the fork's quiesce body and
`pub` on the five declarations the new file reads (`Idle` with its `engine`, `Bytes` with
its `text`, `WithGpu`, `key` and `quiesce`). A test file reading another's fixtures is the
tree's own habit: lane_review_test.zig and lane_rounds_test.zig already take `FakeLearner`
and `LearnBox` out of lane_host_test.zig.

Nothing else changes. Our health_test.zig already imports `posix`, `Threaded`, `listener`,
`auth` and `build_identity`, and its Server.init shape is the one the new test uses.

Gates: both files are in modules test-cuda-host runs (zig/build/cuda.zig:344 runs every
test of core, lanes, api and native; the server tests run through their own module), and
zig build test-rows-host passes with this patch.

What a GPU run must show: nothing. Both are host tests with no device in them.

